q: ==Sine== is defined as the ratio of the ==side opposite to the hypotenuse==.
e: $$\sin{A} = \frac{a}{h}$$ [image:media/trigonometry-triangle.svg]

// @id 01M5AVRFY3DAZC5A2P8S355EVH model=cloze
q: ==Cosine== is defined as the ratio of the ==adjacent leg (the side of the triangle joining the angle to the right angle) to the hypotenuse==.
e: $$\cos{A} = \frac{b}{h}$$ [image:media/trigonometry-triangle.svg]

// @id 01M5AVRFY3X9MEZDS2XHKD6GTR model=cloze
q: ==Tangent== is defined as the ratio of the ==opposite leg to the adjacent leg==.
e: $$\tan{A} = \frac{a}{b}$$ [image:media/trigonometry-triangle.svg]

q: What're the results of negating trigonometric function argument?
a: $$\sin(-x) = -\sin x$$
$$\cos(-x) = \cos x$$
$$\tan(-x) = -\tan x$$
e: Cosine is an even function, while sine and tangent odd functions.

q: What is the trigonometric Pythagorean identity?
a: $$\sin^2 x + \cos^2 x = 1$$

q: What are the sum and difference formulas for trigonometric functions?
a: $$\sin(x \pm y) = \sin x \cos y \pm \cos x \sin y$$
$$\cos(x \pm y) = \cos x \cos y \mp \sin x \sin y$$
$$\tan(x \pm y) = \frac{\tan x \pm \tan y}{1 \mp \tan x \tan y}$$

q: What is the law of sines?
a: $$\frac{\sin A}{a} = \frac{\sin B}{b} = \frac{\sin C}{c} = \frac{2\Delta}{abc}$$ where $\Delta$ is the area of the triangle

q: Whas it the law of cosines?
a: $$c^2 = a^2 + b^2 - 2ab\cos C$$

